    "language_probability": 1,
    "text": "Which brings us to June twenty twenty four. A story exploded across social media. The fifty year petrodollar agreement between America and Saudi Arabia had just expired, and the dollar's reign was over. Millions of people shared it. There was just one problem. There was no fifty year contract to expire. The nineteen seventy four arrangement was never a treaty with an end date. It was a set of understandings, some of them secret, held together by shared interests. And that's actually more important than any contract. Because if the petrodollar runs on interests, not paper, then the real question is, what happens when those interests change?",
